The survey of 2,000 people aged 70 and over, commissioned by the Royal College of Home Carers, shows that:

More than a fifth (21%) of people aged 70 and over said they had been asked to change a patient's bedding, which had previously only been done by a nurse;

At least one-third (34%) had been asked to switch the patient's feeding from a bottle to a spoon;

More than one in five (22%) had been asked to change the patient's bedding from a plastic bag to a cloth.
